---
import Code from "../../components/Code.astro";
import EnrichkitSample from "../../components/EnrichkitSample.astro";
import InstallCommand from "../../components/InstallCommand.astro";
import PluginReference from "../../components/PluginReference.astro";
import { getPlugin } from "../../data/plugins";
import Doc from "../../layouts/Doc.astro";

const plugin = getPlugin("enrichkit")!;

const tocEntries = [
  { id: "what-it-does", text: "What it does", level: 2 as const, children: [] },
  { id: "install", text: "Install", level: 2 as const, children: [] },
  { id: "register", text: "Register", level: 2 as const, children: [] },
  { id: "api-key", text: "Set the API key", level: 2 as const, children: [] },
  { id: "how-it-fires", text: "How it fires", level: 2 as const, children: [] },
  { id: "where-results-go", text: "Where results go", level: 2 as const, children: [] },
  { id: "sample-output", text: "Sample output", level: 2 as const, children: [] },
  { id: "props", text: "Configuration", level: 2 as const, children: [] },
  { id: "for-agents", text: "For agents", level: 2 as const, children: [] },
];
---

<Doc
  tocEntries={tocEntries}
  currentSlug="enrichkit"
  title="enrichkit"
  section="@plugdash/enrichkit"
  description="A summary, tags and a tweet draft for every post, from one LLM call on publish."
>
  <h2 id="what-it-does">What it does</h2>
  <p>
    On publish, enrichkit makes one LLM call (Anthropic or OpenAI) and
    stores a summary, key topics, tags, a reading level and a tweet draft.
    You choose which of the five to generate. The summary also fills an
    empty SEO description. Posts under 100 words are skipped, and
    republishing unchanged text makes no call.
  </p>
  <p>
    There is no companion component. The summary reaches your pages
    through the SEO description; the rest is on the enrichkit admin page
    and in plugin KV for an agent to read.
  </p>

  <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
  <InstallCommand command={plugin.installCommand} />

  <h2 id="register">Register</h2>
  <Code language="js" filename="astro.config.mjs" code={`import { defineConfig } from "astro/config"
import emdash from "emdash/astro"
import { enrichkitPlugin } from "@plugdash/enrichkit"

export default defineConfig({
  integrations: [
    emdash({
      plugins: [
        enrichkitPlugin({ provider: "anthropic" }),
      ],
    }),
  ],
})`} />
  <p>
    <code>provider</code> also sets <code>allowedHosts</code>
    (<code>api.anthropic.com</code> or <code>api.openai.com</code>).
  </p>

  <h2 id="api-key">Set the API key</h2>
  <p>The key is an encrypted plugin setting, so it never lands in your build output.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Generate an encryption key with <code>pnpm exec emdash secrets generate</code>
      and set <code>EMDASH_ENCRYPTION_KEY</code> in the server's process
      environment (on Cloudflare, a Worker secret). A <code>.env</code>
      file alone was not picked up by <code>astro dev</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      In the admin, open <strong>Plugins &gt; enrichkit &gt; Settings</strong>
      and paste your Anthropic or OpenAI key into <strong>API key</strong>.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    The <code>apiKey</code> option also works, but the key ends up in plain
    text in the build. A key in the admin wins over the option.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how-it-fires">How it fires</h2>
  <pre><code>publish -&gt; body &gt;= 100 words -&gt; text changed since last time -&gt; one provider call -&gt; store result</code></pre>
  <ul>
    <li>Only <code>content:afterPublish</code>. Autosaves, draft saves, schedule and unpublish never call the provider.</li>
    <li>Each result keeps a hash of the model, the enrichment flags, the title and the body. Republishing the same text skips the call.</li>
    <li>The reply is structured output. A bad reply, a 429 or a timeout is logged once and not retried; the next changed publish tries again.</li>
    <li>The body is capped at 12,000 characters. A tweet over 280 characters is dropped.</li>
    <li>Nothing fails a publish. Every failure is logged and skipped.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="where-results-go">Where results go</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Plugin KV <code>result:&lt;entry id&gt;</code></strong>, one row per entry, with <code>summary</code>, <code>topics</code>, <code>tags</code>, <code>readingLevel</code>, <code>tweet</code>, <code>model</code>, <code>generatedAt</code> and <code>hash</code>. Only enabled fields are present.</li>
    <li><strong><code>seo.description</code></strong>, when it is empty and <code>writeSeoDescription</code> is on. This goes live at once without a draft. An author's own description is never overwritten.</li>
    <li><strong>The admin page</strong> at Plugins &gt; Enrichkit shows the latest result per entry, with a <strong>Regenerate</strong> button that forces one new call.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="sample-output">Sample output</h2>
  <EnrichkitSample />

  <PluginReference plugin={plugin} />

  <h2 id="for-agents">For agents</h2>
  <p>After installing @plugdash/enrichkit and registering <code>enrichkitPlugin(&#123; provider: "anthropic" &#125;)</code>:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Make sure <code>EMDASH_ENCRYPTION_KEY</code> is set in the server environment, then set the API key under Plugins &gt; enrichkit &gt; Settings.</li>
    <li>Publish a post with at least 100 words of body text.</li>
    <li>Open Plugins &gt; Enrichkit in the admin and check the post has a result, or check the page's meta description now holds the summary.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    If nothing appears, read the server log under the <code>enrichkit</code>
    plugin: <code>no API key</code> means step 1 is missing,
    <code>content unchanged since last enrichment, skipping</code> means the
    hash matched. Data stored: KV <code>result:&lt;entry id&gt;</code> and
    an empty <code>seo.description</code> filled with the summary. The
    stored <code>tweet</code> is there so an agent can post it after a
    human publishes.
  </p>
</Doc>
